From 65225604b00c1db806a05fbc5e6cd027557486cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:43:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 126/274] TileLang V4.1 tests: non-finite contracts

DeepSeek's reference lets a NaN or an infinity through (torch.clamp, relu_,
softmax), so the error that produced it stays visible. Add tolerance-free
checks that the kernels do the same and that a poisoned row moves no other
row:

- exact NaN and signed-infinity positions against the reference for the
  shared SwiGLU, the Engram gate, RoPE, the indexer scores, the BF16 GEMM
  (split-K decode rows included) and sparse MLA;
- a NaN row becomes an all-NaN row with every other row's bits unchanged
  for the block-32 rows GEMM, the WO projection, mHC pre and the routed
  experts;
- sparse MLA reads no record it does not select: every unselected record,
  record 0, the padding and the entries past each list's length hold 0xFF
  bytes, and every route keeps the clean bits.

The routed experts' NaN propagation is a strict xfail: TileKernels' fused
SwiGLU clamps with T.min/T.max, which return the limit for a NaN.

Sparse MLA's setup moves into _mla_case, with the generator calls in the
same order, so test_sparse_mla draws the same inputs.

